// The same rule for the `if` of a guard after a fractional literal
// (spec/01-lexical.md, rows `fractional-suffix` and `suffix-boundary`).
// Before the suffix existed, `case 1.5if t` was the pattern `1.5` with the
// guard `if t`, a valid arm that matched. Now it is the literal `1.5i`, a
// fractional literal with the suffix, and the name `f`: a static error. A
// consumer that has no Int literal yet runs the program, so this probe fails
// today on every consumer and is on each expected-failure list.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
var t = true;
fun pick(x) {
    return match x {
        case 1.5if t => "guarded"
        case _ => "other"
    };
}
print pick(1.5);

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal fractional-suffix
